# Adobe's Core-14 AFM files and their licence are vendored BYTE-EXACT under APAFML, which requires
# that any modification be prominently noted in the modified file and that the licence paragraph
# itself not be modified. Line-ending normalisation is a modification: `MustRead.html` carries the
# original classic-Mac CR endings and the .afm files carry CRLF, and a checkout that rewrote either
# would break the pinned sha256 digests in vendor/afm/README.md and the obligation with them.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion on these paths, whatever the client's core.autocrlf.
vendor/afm/** -text

# Shell scripts run under Git Bash on the Windows release runner, and bash reads a CRLF line's `\r`
# as part of the command. `eol=lf` fixes the checkout ending whatever core.autocrlf a client set,
# so `ci/*.sh` arrives runnable on every clone. `fixtures/gate` needs no line here: git classifies
# all eight PDFs as binary (`git ls-files --eol`), and autocrlf converts only what it takes for text.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Fixtures are engine input, and the engine reads input byte-exact. 42 of the hand-built PDFs under
# fixtures/engine and both RTF files under fixtures/office are plain ASCII with LF endings, so git
# classifies them as text, and a checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites them to CRLF. Measured
# on 5bb78db with such a clone: all 42 PDFs are then refused as malformed, because their
# cross-reference offsets count bytes; both RTFs produce a different artifact; and the PDFs' sha256
# pins in fixtures/manifest.json break.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is Git for Windows' installer default, and GitHub's Windows runners are widely
# reported to check out with it. Neither is verified here, and this entry does not depend on either:
# `-text` holds whatever a client sets.
#
# By directory rather than by extension, as above: what matters is that the bytes are input, not
# which format a later fixture takes. And here rather than as a `core.autocrlf false` step in CI,
# because that would give the runner bytes no Windows clone of this repository gets.
fixtures/** -text
